# arch -- Arch Linux, and what says ID_LIKE=arch (Manjaro, EndeavourOS).
# The same eight keys as debian.env (contract 3). pacman is asked with
# --needed and never -Sy alone: a rolling distro forbids the partial
# upgrade, so a package the box's database no longer finds is a todo
# naming `sudo pacman -Syu`. Every name here is credited in CREDITS.md.
PM=pacman
PM_INSTALL=sudo pacman -S --needed
PM_TARGET=Arch Linux
# core -- the AI: SITE_SHELL=off installs only these (+ PKG_AI for vulkan);
# python is python3 on Arch
PKG_CORE=git curl ca-certificates python
# llama.cpp's build needs OpenMP: gcc-libs ships it, and is in base already
PKG_ENGINE=gcc-libs
# the vulkan build only: the loader and Mesa's two drivers (what Debian's
# mesa-vulkan-drivers holds; nothing here is sized to one machine)
PKG_AI=vulkan-icd-loader vulkan-radeon vulkan-intel
# the shell layer -- SITE_SHELL=on (spark shell on): tmux, the font's
# unzip + fc-cache, a tmux-256color terminfo (ncurses), checkupdates
# for the pending row (pacman-contrib)
# (diffutils: install.sh compares a rendered file with cmp; kbd: setvtrgb
# for the console palette unit -- Arch's base has neither)
PKG_SHELL=bash tmux unzip fontconfig ncurses pacman-contrib diffutils kbd
# the shell's daily tools (fd and bat keep their names here)
PKG_CLI=bat eza fzf zoxide ripgrep fd jq btop
